      "traceTextDiagram": "CAS Garbage Collection with Pin Protection\n├── GC() entrypoint \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:17\n│   ├── List all CAS objects \u003c-- 6a\n│   ├── For each object: \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:29\n│   │   ├── Check if pinned \u003c-- 6b\n│   │   │   └── Skip if KeepPinned \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:35\n│   │   ├── Check age criteria \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:39\n│   │   │   └── Skip if too recent \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:40\n│   │   └── Attempt removal \u003c-- 6c\n│   │       └── Remove(ctx, digest) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:48\n│   └── Return GCResult \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/gc.go:68\n└── Remove() safety checks \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/sqlite_store.go:350\n    ├── Query pinned status \u003c-- 6d\n    ├── Reject if pinned \u003c-- 6e\n    │   └── return ErrPinned \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/cas/sqlite_store.go:369\n    └── DELETE from cas_objects \u003c-- 6f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen named memories or cache entries store large artifacts (like file contents or command outputs), those artifacts are stored in a **content-addressed storage (CAS)** system. The problem: if you naively delete old CAS objects to reclaim disk space, you might accidentally delete artifacts that are still referenced by active memories or cache entries, breaking those references.\n\nThe solution is **pinning**: when a memory or cache entry is saved, it \"pins\" its referenced artifacts [1f], marking them as protected. When the memory is deleted, those artifacts are \"unpinned\" [2f]. Garbage collection then respects these pins, skipping pinned objects [6b] and only removing truly unreferenced artifacts [6f].\n\n## Details\n\n**CAS garbage collection** starts by listing all stored objects [6a]. For each object, it checks whether the object is pinned [6b, 6d]. If `KeepPinned` is enabled and the object has `pinned=1` in the database, GC skips it to protect referenced artifacts.\n\nThe **Remove operation has a safety guard**: even if GC tries to delete a pinned object, Remove queries the pinned status [6d] and returns `ErrPinned` [6e] if the object is still protected. Only unpinned objects are actually deleted from the `cas_objects` table [6f].\n\n**Age-based filtering** is also supported: GC can skip objects newer than a cutoff time, allowing you to preserve recent artifacts regardless of pin status.\n\nThe pinning mechanism creates a **reference counting system** where:\n- Memory saves increment the pin count [1f]\n- Memory deletes decrement the pin count [2f]  \n- GC respects the pin count to avoid premature deletion [6b]\n\nThis ensures that artifacts remain available as long as any memory or cache entry references them, while still allowing cleanup of truly orphaned objects."
    }
